Z-Score:(known standard deviation)

1. It is the process of measuring how many standard deviations a data point is from
the mean.

2. Formula --->   z= (actual_data_point - mean)/std_deviation

3. It will be normally distributed data

4. outcome:

    4.1 Positive Score(value is above the mean)
    4.2 Negative Score(value is below the mean)

T - Score:(unkmown standard deviation)

almost the replica of the z-score but it is used when dont know the
standard deviation.

F- Score:

IT is process finding difference in variance withing the group and between the group

